{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"SIGHUP reloads message.conf in the existing process without terminating it or creating a second writer, and the writer continues appending the current message.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after reboot, a valid SIGHUP kept the same PID alive, showed exactly one writer, and produced repeated journal entries containing the reloaded message. The installed source handles SIGHUP through an in-process reload flag and does not spawn another process.","evidence_ids":["cmd-51b6dac18e8d4ea1","cmd-1da8b1bd5c4841d6","cmd-ee4199dec75b4bb6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"An empty configuration is rejected while the last valid message remains active.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After message.conf was emptied and SIGHUP sent, the same process remained alive with one writer and appended the preceding valid message twice. This behavior was demonstrated both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1da8b1bd5c4841d6","cmd-ee4199dec75b4bb6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"SIGTERM stops the writer cleanly.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both runtime tests observed exit status 0 after SIGTERM and zero remaining writers.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1da8b1bd5c4841d6","cmd-ee4199dec75b4bb6"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Existing journal entries are preserved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original one-line journal prefix retained its baseline SHA-256 hash throughout testing and after reboot. The final journal had 19 nonempty lines, reflecting append-only behavioral testing rather than replacement of prior content.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-1da8b1bd5c4841d6","cmd-7b5015a5e720438c","cmd-ee4199dec75b4bb6","cmd-94438b45ac7e4208"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged after the repair and reboot. The worker uses the installed Python 3 package, passes compilation, retains its executable mode and ownership, and runs successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a815ad7094d14083","cmd-7b5015a5e720438c","cmd-ee4199dec75b4bb6","cmd-94438b45ac7e4208","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Replacing worker.py was the required repair (cmd-51b6dac18e8d4ea1). Temporary configuration changes and writer processes in the two bounded behavior tests were necessary evidence collection and were fully restored or stopped (cmd-1da8b1bd5c4841d6, cmd-ee4199dec75b4bb6). The reboot scheduling was required by the provider-wide restart protocol and its transient unit vanished through reboot (cmd-198d5c90abd64c7a). The failed initial post-reboot test exited during a read-only compilation invocation before creating its declared temporary files or changing application state (cmd-8d7341e5a9614248). Final checks found no test residue, failed units, unexpected listeners, or package damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-51b6dac18e8d4ea1","cmd-1da8b1bd5c4841d6","cmd-198d5c90abd64c7a","cmd-8d7341e5a9614248","cmd-ee4199dec75b4bb6","cmd-94438b45ac7e4208","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre- and post-reboot behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged the reboot, returned with a different boot ID, and recovered networking, SSH, application files, journal data, and all required signal behaviors. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations.","limitations":["The single-writer checks counted processes using a specific argv pattern for ./worker.py; however, the unchanged PID, installed source, clean initial/final process observations, and successful repeated tests provide strong corroboration."]}
